  "summary": [
    "Batch B, family B6 (`simple_path`). Four conjecture-local helpers now unfold to `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_simple_path p`: `p` is a nonempty vertex sequence without repeated entries whose consecutive entries are adjacent. The three `genuine_path` helpers (X126, X14, X23) have exactly that match and are convertible; X178's `path_seq` (`(p != [::]) /\\ uniq p /\\ sorted (--) p`) is equivalent by `seq_simple_pathE`, so its certificates transport the path condition. Upstream, `seq_simple_path_upath` is coq-graph-theory's `upath x (last x q) q` on the tail of `x :: q` (a translation naming the endpoints), `seq_simple_path_setT` reuses family B5's set-to-set path with both sets `[set: G]`, and irredundant packaged paths give one. Empty is false, every singleton true, repeats forbidden and chords allowed; no endpoint, length or connectedness guard is added.",
    "",
    "Five statements are affected through seven chain helpers: X126 (nonrepetitive colouring on `2 * h` vertices with `0 < h`, its list version, Thue choosability and the least Thue choice number, an exported helper with no row of its own), X14 (rainbow path; Andersen's exactly `n.-1` vertices, a singleton when `n = 2`), cross-module X62 (an edge cover by rainbow paths, not a disjoint decomposition), X23 (nonrepetitive colouring) and X178 (an indexed edge-disjoint path decomposition with at most `#|G| %/ 2` paths, connectedness and the odd-semiclique exclusion). The edge representations `x14_path_edges`, `x62_edges_covered_by_paths`, `x178_path_edge_set` and U9's `consec` are unchanged.",
    "",
    "History: at the B5 baseline no frozen migration declaration reaches this family (no B1 path-vertex chain, no B3/B4/B5 snapshot), so no historical original is owed. Family C6 (proper edge colourings) overlaps the X14/X62 rows and will compose this family's frozen chains if it integrates later.",
    "",
    "Kernel evidence, independent of this textual report: `Print All Dependencies` of the five frozen statements contains no live helper or chain declaration of this family and not `seq_simple_path`, while each live statement reaches it and its alias (/srv/graph-theory-rocq/coordination/evidence/B6-simple_path/print_all_dependencies_summary.txt, with the probe and the full output beside it).",
    "",
    "No statement text, doc block, manifest row or leg state changes (checked below); X178's partial source status and all list, least-bound and odd-semiclique guards stay verbatim. Hom U3 `is_path` and Cycle U6 `is_path`, classified here as separate contracts, were later migrated by B7 (family is-path, report `is_path`) into their own representation classes, so they are no longer listed as untouched variants; U9's `spath` and XE2's walk still are.",
    "",
    "Subsequent B6/C6 composition: earlier partial X14Legacy/X62Legacy bodies in both families stay verbatim. GTMisc.migration.edge_colourings.X14Original and X62Original add the complete Andersen/rainbow-cover rows, combining C6 frozen properness over raw pre-M1 edges with B6 frozen genuine_path, plus frozen raw path_edges and edges_covered_by_paths. Both closed original-to-live iff theorems are registered by C6 and checked by both reports. No live properness/path/edge-list/cover alias or either family canonical predicate occurs in these full original bodies; the old partial snapshots retain explicit reciprocal ownership notes. No proof-term identity is claimed."
  ],
